<Page title="About AmpExam: Free Journeyman Electrician Exam Prep" description="AmpExam is a free site with NEC based practice questions for the journeyman and master electrician exams, from conduit fill to grounding.">
  <p>{site.BRAND} is an independent site. {site.author.bio}</p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>Journeyman and master electrician exams pull heavily from the National Electrical Code, and most candidates fail not on theory but on code-book navigation under time pressure. Our practice sets are built around that: conduit fill calculations, box fill, grounding and bonding, and load calculations, each tied to the NEC article and table it comes from so you can find it fast on test day.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>We work from the current NEC edition adopted in each state and the state licensing board's exam content outline. Articles on this site are written with AI assistance and then verified against the code book and board materials before publishing, a process described fully in our <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a>. Where a state has amended a code section, we note the amendment separately from the base NEC text.</p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>Practice questions and guides are free to use. Revenue comes from affiliate commissions when readers buy code books, tool kits, or licensed prep courses through links on the site. Terms are in our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Code adoption dates and table numbers change between cycles. Report an error through <a href="/contact/">contact</a> and we'll correct and date it.</p>
</Page>
